model g6_refusal_order
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
  note "T, issue #55, G6: which refusal a place keeps (E §4.1, E §4.2 step 4; tally 2.1.2's text order, #57 asks the spec): two plan moves a and ab, one leg each on one day into gone after its lifespan ends (RUN-LIFESPAN), both refused at src. src keeps the first refusal booked, and the day's plan legs are booked in their order's text, where ab's sorts before a's (b before the separator), so bal(src) prints ab.cash; the typed movement order would print a.cash. Its twin books ab into keep, alive, so a.cash refuses alone."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

move a: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

move ab: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
